    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0304" n="292" xml:id="pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/190</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Chief of the Division
                        of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Alling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-15">April 15, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Davallou<anchor n="11" xml:id="d330-f1"/> called and stated that, in the
                    absence of the Minister from Washington, he had been instructed to bring to our
                    notice the contents of a telegram which he had received from the Prime Minister.
                    Mr. Davallou referred to the conversation which the Iranian Minister had had
                    with the Acting Secretary on Saturday,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d330-f2"/> in which
                    the Minister pointed out the serious difficulties which the Prime Minister was
                    encountering with the Mejliss in his efforts to bring about the expulsion of the
                    Japanese Legation from Tehran. The Prime Minister had now instructed the
                    Legation to state that it would assist him greatly in his dealings with the
                    Mejliss if he could make public announcement of the fact that Iran had been
                    found eligible for Lend-Lease by the United States. Mr. Davallou stressed again
                    and again the importance which such an announcement would have in strengthening
                    the position of the Prime Minister.</p>
                <p>I assured Mr. Davallou that I fully understood the point he was making and that I
                    would be glad to bring the matter to the attention of the interested officials
                    in the Department.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d330-f1" n="11" xml:id="d330-f1-content">
                <p>H. Hadjeb-Davallou, First Secretary of the Iranian Legation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d330-f2" n="12" xml:id="d330-f2-content">
